WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:14.000
A rebalance resizes each slot toward its share of the current IM limit. It sells more where there is room and buys back where the book is too large.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:27.000
Start with the dry run. It lists what the pass would do, slot by slot. It sends nothing and records no change.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:42.000
Read the risk before you confirm. Selling more adds premium and the risk of a big move. Buying back pays the asking price, the spread and fees.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:56.000
A slot can stay short of its share. The liquidity cap, a stop hold or the size cap can limit it, and the list says which.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:15.000
The real pass reads fresh margin, so its orders can differ from the preview. An order that does not fill in time is cancelled, and the rest is tried later.
